# 4. Consumer electronics

This is where ordinary life changes most visibly.

## 1930s–1940s
- portable radios become common much earlier;
- hearing aids shrink dramatically;
- car radios become cheaper;
- battery-powered electronics expand;
- public-address, police, aviation, and maritime radios improve;
- early transistorized hi-fi equipment appears.

Portable radio changes politics and culture. Cheap receivers make mass broadcasting more personal and harder to control. Authoritarian states still jam signals, but citizens can listen privately.

